ok   eig of a real matrix with all-real eigenvalues returns a REAL dtype (documented 'unless the imaginary part is zero in which case it will be cast to a real type')
ok   eig of the defective matrix [[1,1],[0,1]]: eigenvalues [1,1], eigenvector matrix rank 1 (documented 'may not be of maximum rank')  (eigenvectors [[1.0, -1.0], [0.0, 0.0]])
