ok   eig dtypes: float32 -> float32 eigenvalues (real case) / complex64 (complex case), vectors float32; complex64 -> complex64; int -> float64  (float32 5x5 -> complex64)
ok   eig float32 eigenvalues agree with mpmath to 1e-5 relative
ok   eig with NaN input raises LinAlgError (source _assert_finite; docstring lists only non-convergence)
ok   eig complex (4,4): eigenvalues match mpmath, A v = w v, unit-norm vectors
---- eigh / eigvalsh
ok   eigvalsh(UPLO='L', default) on a NON-symmetric input uses the lower triangle (eigenvalues of tril+tril^T from mpmath.eigsy, ascending)
