ok   eigh(UPLO='L'/'U') eigenvalues ascending (documented) and match the same triangle rule; V diag(w) V^T reconstructs the symmetrised triangle
ok   eigh eigenvectors orthonormal, unit norm (documented 'normalized eigenvector')
ok   eigh/eigvalsh reject UPLO other than 'L'/'U' (ValueError)
ok   eigh complex Hermitian: real ascending eigenvalues match mpmath.eighe; V^H V = I; V diag(w) V^H = H
ok   eigh/eigvalsh ignore the imaginary part of the diagonal (documented 'imaginary part of the diagonal will always be treated as zero')
ok   eigvalsh on a stack (3,4,4): row i = eigenvalues of A[i] (mpmath)
